    {
      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Blue: the Ravel CLI, with its runner inside. Grey: child group and terminal.\nA and B are alternative outcomes. B can begin before exec. A1 and A2 are alternative recovery rules within A.\nThe X belongs only to A: confirmed child reap. It does not mark the group’s disappearance or a reap in B.\nAnother group can hold delegated foreground. The holder notes show when Ravel preserves it or reclaims it.\nHandback and mode restoration temporarily ignore SIGTTOU, then restore its prior disposition. Ravel checks these operations.\nForeground query and handback are not atomic. CLI lifetime establishes neither of B’s two conditions.\nAfter failed spawn, the attempted group ID never authorises numeric signals. Unknown status does not permit wider takeover.\nRecovery errors return no result to the caller. Cancellation can override the original failure, but keeps recovery reports.",
      "x": 340.0,
      "y": 1654.4457031250006,
      "anchor": "center",
      "align": "center",
      "wrapped": true,
      "w": 640.0,
      "h": 267.35078125000007
    }
